Correction: "dl" and "tl" are permitted in Lojban if the two consonants are=
 in=20
different syllables, but not if they are both in the onset of the same=20
syllable. E.g. "fatlutfa'i", "badle'o". "dl" is a permitted initial in=20
Russian; I don't know for sure about "tl".

Irregularities in the list of permitted combinations and permitted initials=
:=20
"ms" is permitted but "mz" is not; "cm", "cn", and "jm" are permitted initi=
als=20
but "jn" is not; similarly "zn".

Some pairs of gismu differ by exchanging two letters and are similar in=20
meaning: ractu/ratcu, stuzi/stizu, garna/grana. Other groups of gismu diffe=
r in=20
one letter and are similar in meaning: carce/marce/karce, culno/mulno.

Some sets of cmavo are phonetically related (zi, za, zu); others are not=20
(du'a, be'a, vu'a, ne'u). The ko'a-series and fo'a-series are phonetically=
=20
related but should not be, as within each series, they differ in the unstre=
ssed=20
vowel, making it easy to mistake which sumti one is referring to.

The symmetry of the logical conjunction matrix is broken by the sentence=20
separator.

